  "_about": "STEGOSAURUS STENOPS (sculpt overlay, 2026-11-05): 7 m -- hind legs twice the fore, the back peaked high over the hips and falling to a tiny long low head carried under a metre up; 17 rounded-pentagonal plates in two staggered rows along the spine, the largest (.65 m) over the hips and the root of the tail; the tail held off the ground, ending in the thagomizer's four spikes pointing out and back. Countershaded olive, the plates flushed rust with darker rims. (2026-11-08, plates.py) The PLATES are `fin` sheets (they were a flat ell and a cone each: orange cones, the front ones buried in the back): 19 in two staggered rows from the neck to the middle of the tail, each leaning out 10 degrees, rooted along the back's surface, small and rounded on the neck, largest over the hips and the base of the tail, more pointed down the tail; thin with a sharp rim on an exact pentagonal outline, thickened and faired into the back at the base, grooved (`finrays` fanning from the base) and darker toward the rim; each rides the spine or tail bone it stands on. The thagomizer's spikes stay horns.",
